e for 1972 European Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/60536"} "Ivan Yarygin"] ", who won all seven of his matches by falls. He needed only 17:03 on the mat to win his gold medal decisively. Silver went to Mongolian " [:a {:href "/athletes/59395"} "Khorloogiin Bayanmönkh"] ", who had been runner-up at the 1971 Worlds. He won that medal with a victory on points over Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/58553"} "József Csátári"] ", who had also won a bronze medal at the 1968 Olympics, that one in light-heavyweight freestyle."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Yarygin would win the 1973 World Championships, the 1975-76 Europeans, and defended his Olympic gold medal in 1976 at Montréal. Bayanmönkh also wrestled at the 1976 Olympics, placing fifth in heavyweight freestyle."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "382"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60536"} "Ivan Yarygin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "232"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59395"} "Khorloogiin Bayanmönkh"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MGL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MGL.png"}] "MGL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "143"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58553"} "József Csatári"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://